WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.210
- [Instructor] If I were to ask you,

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.160
what is five

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:09.850
minus three plus two?

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.670
What would you say that is?

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.503
Pause this video and
try to figure that out.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.640
All right, well if you
wanted to tackle this,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.810
you would really just read
it from left to right,

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.780
or you would compute
it from left to right.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.010
You'd first figure out
what five minus three is,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.890
and five minus three is equal to two.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:30.450
And so you'd say, okay,
that's going to be two

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:35.450
plus two, which of course
we know is equal to four.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.220
Now, what if I were to
involve a little bit

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.300
of multiplication or division?

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.380
If I were to go up to
you and I were to say,

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.360
what is five

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.660
plus three times two?

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.860
Pause this video and
try to figure that out.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.350
Well, you might be tempted
to do it in a similar way.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.470
You might be tempted to say,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.400
okay, I'll just go from left to right.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.860
I'll first compute what five plus three is

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:06.560
and that of course,
would be equal to eight,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.950
and then I would multiply eight times two

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.100
to get 16.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.280
But it turns out that this

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:15.960
would not be the right
way to approach this,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:17.740
because for very good reasons

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:20.490
that we'll study in perhaps future videos,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.130
we don't always go left to right,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.230
especially when we're dealing

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.490
with different types of operations.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.440
And the standard way
that this is approached

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.390
is that multiplication
and division will be done

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.860
before addition and subtraction.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.780
So the way that you would
actually compute this

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:41.970
is that you would compute
the three times two first.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.600
So you would say that
this is the same thing

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.160
as five plus six,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:51.160
five plus six, which is going
to be equal to 11, not 16.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:57.010
So this is going to be equal to 11.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:58.410
So with that out of the way,

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.210
let's do a few more examples.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.810
Let's say someone were
to approach you and say,

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.100
what is nine

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:11.100
minus six divided by three?

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:14.193
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.560
Well, as I just said, we would
do multiplication or division

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:21.610
before we do subtraction.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:25.030
So we'll actually do the
six divided by three first,

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:27.640
and six divided by three is two.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:31.830
So this simplifies to nine minus two,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.490
which is equal to seven,

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:35.030
and I really wanna emphasize,

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.320
it's important that you get this idea

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.840
that multiplication and
division should be done

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.240
before the addition or subtraction,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.120
unless you're given some
other types of directions.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.800
Because if you just
went left to right here,

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:48.700
you would have said
nine minus six is three,

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.300
and then you would've
divided that by three,

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.400
which would have given you one,

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:56.170
which is clearly a
different number than seven.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.770
Let's do one more example, just for kicks.

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.020
Let's say that someone were to ask you,

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.510
what is two

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:09.550
times three minus one?

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:12.580
Pause the video and try
to figure that one out.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.090
Well, in this one, doing
our multiplication first

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.200
is also the same as going
left to right first.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.710
So if we do two times three first,

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.200
two times three is six,

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:23.260
so that's six,

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.610
and then we would wanna
calculate six minus one,

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.140
which is of course equal to five.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.730
So big picture, if you
just have a bunch of things

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:34.590
that are being added, subtracted,
multiply, and divided,

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.880
and there is no parenthesis in it,

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.510
you would always prioritize
the multiplication

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:44.303
or the division over the
addition or the subtraction.

